      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 42-year-old woman was seen with an inspiratory stridor and expiratory wheezing. The wheezing responded quickly to asthma treatment. The stridor, however, was caused by a significant narrowing of the trachea between the branching of a tracheal bronchus ('bronchus suis' or ' pig bronchus') and the main carina."},
